it was supposed to be a relaxing morning  playing America's national pastime  instead the US Capitol is reeling after  a hail of gunfire just outside of  Washington a gunman opened fire at this  field targeting a gathering of  Republican congressman and others  practicing for a baseball game he  wounded several people before being shot  dead by police one of those hit was  Louisiana Congressman Steve Scalise the  number three Republican in the US House  of Representatives he's recovering at a  nearby hospital  the auto look at Scalise colleague and  top-ranking House Republican Paul Ryan  praised the police response  he called for unity in the wake of the  shooting I asked each of you to join me  to resolve to come together to lift each  other up and to show the country to show  the world that we are one house the  people's house United in our humanity it  is that humanity which will win the day  and it always will god bless I yield US  officials have identified the assailant  as this man 66 year-old James Hodge  Kison from the state of Illinois  authorities say it's too early to say  whether the incident was politically  motivated but eyewitnesses to the  shooting have lamented the country's  deep divides  you can't have this sort of political  division in the nation like America that  we should accept other people's views  and not target them with ak-47 earlier  mass shootings in the u.s. have often  triggered renewed debate about gun  control in the country  but it's unclear whether this latest  incident will have a similar effect  Scalise himself is a fierce advocate for  gun rights and previous debates on the  issue have often only deepened political  divides
 

